From cf134c4046ca802aa8b4d85be8ae6d1dd7a7acdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:44:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Efficiency ratios, SG&A line name, book value growth; one
 basis for balance ratios

- Inventory and payables turnover and days against cost of sales on average
  balances, and the cash conversion cycle (DSO + DIO - DPO).
- SG&A is derived from selling_and_distribution_expense, the catalog key (the
  calculator only knew selling_distribution_expense, so SG&A was never derived).
- book_value_growth: book value per share against the prior year end.
- capex to D&A falls back to the cash-flow D&A add-back when no income-statement
  D&A is reported.
- In a year (or the year after one) with discontinued operations, continuing-
  operations flows exclude a business the opening balances still hold, so
  turnover, days, ROIC, ROCE, asset/fixed-asset/working-capital turnover and
  incremental ROIC are withheld. These rows are refreshed by the build-end
  reconciliation like the comparisons.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
