From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:44:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] SABIC statement lines, balances 2020-2023, ownership
 history, release volumes

- AR2025 statements and notes 20/32/33/39 (figures matched on their pages):
  capex 2025 as PPE + intangibles (as 2019-2024), cash-flow D&A, zakat and tax,
  EBIT 2024, NCI share of profit, other reserves, 2023 equity as restated (note
  42), 2024 weighted shares, key management compensation, bank guarantees.
- Zakat and income tax stored as an expense (negative), the engine convention,
  in the 2019-2025 statement manifests.
- Balances: 2020 (Q4 2021 report), 2021-2022 (2022 FS), 2023 (2023 FS, text
  matched): inventories, trade receivables and payables, cash, debt, totals,
  statutory reserve; subtotals checked.
- AR2025 five-year table: the 2021-2023 'cash' rows were the cash-flow closing
  cash (2023: 33.80 bn vs 32.41 bn on the balance sheet) and duplicated cash_end;
  removed, balance-sheet cash now comes from the statements.
- Ownership: PIF 70% / public 30% at 2019-12-31 (Q4 2019 note 1); board and senior
  executives' SABIC shares at 2025-12-31 as an insider class total (pp.119-120).
- FY2025 release: adjusted EBIT and adjusted EPS 2025/2024; Q3 2026 release:
  sales volumes by product line, segment and Specialties.

